---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL, LINKS } from '../lib/brand';
const contact = LEGAL.contactEmail
  ? `email ${LEGAL.contactEmail}`
  : 'use the contact page';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy" description="What data Baken and baken.ca collect, where it goes, and what stays on your own machine.">
  <p>
    Baken is built so that the data your agents work with stays on hardware you control. This page describes
    exactly what the Baken apps and the baken.ca website collect, who processes it, and what you can do about it.
    {LEGAL.operator} ("we") operates baken.ca and publishes the Baken apps. We are based in {LEGAL.location}.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There is no Baken account and no Baken server holding your conversations, memory or files.</li>
    <li>Your agent's memory and history live on the host machine you run.</li>
    <li>The release builds of the apps contain no crash reporting or analytics.</li>
    <li>baken.ca uses self-hosted, cookie-free analytics to count visits.</li>
    <li>If you connect a cloud model, that provider receives what your agent sends it, under its own terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Baken apps</h2>
  <h3>Data that stays on your hardware</h3>
  <p>
    Conversations, agent memory, files, tool output and settings are stored on the host machine you run, and on your
    paired phone or desktop as a local cache. We do not receive a copy. Agent memory is kept as plain text files on the
    host, which you can read, edit, back up or delete directly.
  </p>

  <h3>How your devices connect</h3>
  <p>
    Your phone or desktop connects to your host over Iroh, a peer-to-peer protocol. The connection is encrypted end to
    end with keys held only by your paired devices. It goes direct when it can. When a direct path is not available,
    traffic passes through a public relay operated by n0, the maintainers of Iroh. A relay can see the IP addresses
    involved and the volume and timing of traffic, but it cannot read the content. You can configure your host to use
    your own relay or to disable relays.
  </p>

  <h3>Model providers</h3>
  <p>
    Baken can use local models or cloud models. With a local model, prompts and responses stay on your hardware. With a
    cloud model (for example from OpenAI, Anthropic or Google), your agent sends prompts, context and tool results to that
    provider, which processes them under its own privacy policy and terms. You choose and configure the provider; we have
    no access to that traffic.
  </p>

  <h3>Telemetry and crash reports</h3>
  <p>
    The published release builds of the apps do not include crash reporting or usage analytics. The source contains
    optional integrations for crash reporting (Sentry) and performance monitoring (Kotzilla) that are used only in
    developer builds where a developer supplies their own configuration. Crash details are written to a file on your own
    device so you can read or share them yourself; they are not sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h3>Permissions</h3>
  <p>
    The Android app asks for the camera to scan pairing codes, the microphone for voice mode, and notifications for task
    updates. Each is used only for that purpose, and you can deny or revoke any of them in system settings.
  </p>

  <h2>The baken.ca website</h2>
  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    baken.ca uses Umami, an open source analytics tool that we host ourselves. It records page views, the referring site,
    browser and device type, country, and clicks on download buttons. It sets no cookies and does not build a profile of
    you across sites. Visit data stays on our own server.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting</h3>
  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare. As part of delivering and protecting the site, Cloudflare processes request data such
    as your IP address and browser details, under its own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h3>Links and downloads</h3>
  <p>
    Downloads and source code are hosted on GitHub. When you follow those links, GitHub's privacy policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Most of your data never reaches us, so you control it directly on your own hardware. For the limited website data we
    hold, you can ask what we have, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to its use. To make a request, {contact}.
    We will respond within 30 days. If you are in Canada you may also contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
    Canada; if you are in the EU or UK, your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Baken is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how data is handled, we will update this page and the date at the top. The source for this page is
    public in the <a href={LINKS.webRepo}>baken-web repository</a>, so every change is visible in its history.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
